    {
      "segment_id": "S00001",
      "start_char": 0,
      "end_char": 155,
      "text": "MEXICO\nAnnex XII. Recent Reforms in Tax Administration\nA focus on improving tax administration and compliance under the current government has resulted in\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00002",
      "start_char": 155,
      "end_char": 348,
      "text": "a wide range of reforms have contributed to the strong revenue performance through recent shocks.\nHowever, further revenue gains in this area may be harder to obtain as non-compliant behaviors\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00003",
      "start_char": 348,
      "end_char": 534,
      "text": "adapt, the base of erosion and evasion narrows, and remaining issues require more complex solutions.\n1. Improving tax administration has been a central pillar of the government’s fiscal\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00004",
      "start_char": 534,
      "end_char": 707,
      "text": "policy agenda. Under the current administration, revenue mobilization efforts in Mexico have\ncentered on improving tax compliance. Notable reforms since 2019 have included:\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00005",
      "start_char": 707,
      "end_char": 862,
      "text": "• The abolition of the right to offset excess tax credits against other taxes, building on staff\nrecommendations regarding tackling large-scale tax fraud;\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00006",
      "start_char": 862,
      "end_char": 1066,
      "text": "• The requirement that digital platforms withhold taxes due on transactions in which they acted as\nintermediary;\n• Implementation of General Anti-Abuse Rules (GAAR) and the prohibition of company mergers\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00007",
      "start_char": 1066,
      "end_char": 1302,
      "text": "for tax purposes to tackle corporate tax planning; and\n• Enaction of actions 2, 4 and 12 in the OECD’s Base Erosion and Profit Shifting (BEPS) agenda.\n2. Administration reforms may have supported revenue performance in recent years but\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00008",
      "start_char": 1302,
      "end_char": 1483,
      "text": "returns to efforts are expected to moderate over the medium-term. Since 2019, income and\ncorporate tax and VAT revenues have grown as a share of GDP, with expected increases of 1.0\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00009",
      "start_char": 1483,
      "end_char": 1671,
      "text": "and 0.6 percent of GDP between 2019 and 2022, respectively. This strong revenue performance\nis deemed to be at least partially due to the bedding-in of compliance policies and analysis of\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00010",
      "start_char": 1671,
      "end_char": 1851,
      "text": "the VAT gap undertaken by the authorities suggests a reduction in VAT evasion of around\nMEX$170 billion between 2018 and 2021. However, given the successive shocks that Mexico has\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00011",
      "start_char": 1851,
      "end_char": 2047,
      "text": "faced as well as changes to the structure of the labor market due to other reforms, isolating the\nimpact of these measures is difficult, particularly given the deterrent effect that they may have\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00012",
      "start_char": 2047,
      "end_char": 2231,
      "text": "had on taxpayer behavior. The effect of efforts in this area may run into diminishing returns due\nto adaptation of non-compliance behavior and, possibly, a smaller base of evasion and\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00013",
      "start_char": 2231,
      "end_char": 2420,
      "text": "avoidance from which additional revenues can be obtained. The authorities’ new focus on non-\ncompliance at the border may also represent a tougher challenge given the overlap with security\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00014",
      "start_char": 2420,
      "end_char": 2602,
      "text": "issues and the need for close coordination between the tax administration and the army, which\nhas taken over the physical customs inspection functions.\n86 INTERNATIONAL MONETARY FUND"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "schema_version": "locator_index_v1",
